    "title": "Strong wind; mountain snow overnight - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Haley Bouley ,\n2 hours ago Now that the cold front has cruised through the region, our northwest to westerly wind is picking up in intensity. Especially in Southern Vermont, winds will be strong potentially knocking out power as the reach gusts to 50+ mph. For Central and Northern Vermont gust won’t be quite as extreme, climb to 35-45 mph at times. Charge your devices now, in case you lose power overnight. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 1",
